 "title": "Office of the Recorder - HomePage",
 "text": "Office of the Recorder - HomePage\nSkip to main content Enable accessibility for low vision Open the accessibility menu\nOffice of the Recorder\nClermont County, Ohio\nAbout Us\nAbout the Recorder\nHistory of the Recorder's Office\nRecorders Throughout History\nPublic Records and Retention Policy\nSearch Records\nSearch Online Records\nSearch Instructions\nFraudSleuth\nRecording\nHow to Record a Document\nDocument Standards\nDocuments Recorded\nE-Filing\nFee Schedule\nForms\nVeteran Information\nGood Deeds\nI Want To...\nPress Releases\nLinks\n\" alt=\"\" role=\"presentation\" data-uw-rm-alt-original=\"Office of the Recorder\" data-uw-rm-alt-hash=\"3338908027751811\" data-uw-rm-alt=\"SRC\">\nDocuments Recorded\nReal Estate Search\nFee Schedule\nFor two hundred years the Clermont County Recorder’s office has recorded and archived every document dealing with land, titles, and land ownership within the county borders. Records maintained by the office have gone from the quill pen to computer image. Today we stand ready to faithfully discharge the duties of recording, archiving, and making readily accessible all land transactions within our county. Many records are accessible through this website and the rest are maintained physically at the Recorder’s office in Batavia, Ohio. We are dedicated to serving you.\nTim Rudd Clermont County Recorder\nTim Rudd, Clermont County Recorder in conjunction with Common Pleas Court Probate Judge James A. Shriver and the Common Pleas Clerk Allen Freeman would like to announce the Good Deeds Program. The Good Deeds Program provides steps to allow you to minimize or even avoid your exposure to the costs associated with Probate Court . Click on the Good Deeds tab to learn more.\nProtect your property for free. Sign up for FraudSlueth to receive alerts when anyone has filed a document regarding your property in Clermont County. Click on the FraudSlueth tab to learn more.\nThe Clermont County Recorder issues Veteran ID cards to all honorably discharged veterans with proper documentation. The cards are free and so is the recording of your DD-214. Click on the Veteran Tab for more information or stop in and see us during office hours.\n101 East Main St.\nBatavia, OH 45103\nOffice: 513.732.7236\nFax: 513.732.7891\nContact Us\nHoliday Closures\nSecurity and Privacy Policy\nAccessibility",
